## Project Overview

This project extends the xv6 operating system with multiple security mechanisms designed for medical device environments.

The project implements:

- User authentication and role management
- Password hashing
- Login enforcement
- File ownership and permissions
- chmod and chown system calls
- Kernel syscall audit logging
- Root-only audit access
- Automated medical compliance testing

## Implemented Phases

### Phase 1 — Authentication System
- whoami syscall
- useradd syscall
- userdel syscall
- passwd syscall
- login syscall
- Role switching and authentication

### Phase 2 — File Access Control
- File owner metadata
- File permission metadata
- chmod syscall
- chown syscall
- Permission enforcement in sys_open

### Phase 3 — Audit Logging
- Kernel audit ring buffer
- Syscall activity logging
- auditread syscall
- Root-only audit access

### Bonus Phase — Compliance Testing
- Automated security validation using medtest
- Full integration testing for all security mechanisms

## Technologies Used

- xv6-public
- C Programming
- QEMU
- GCC
- Git & GitHub
- Kali Linux

## Repository Branches

- main → Phase 1
- phase2 → File permissions
- phase3 → Audit logging
- bonus → Compliance testing

## Final Result

The final system simulates a secure medical-device operating system with authentication, access control, auditing, and compliance validation mechanisms.
